  data:  # 04c7
    kind: invariant  # 04c7
    title: "A function_summaries.d file declaring provenance: community loads as YOURS: stamped user_supplied, ranked above built-in, kept by --no-default-overlays"  # 04c7
    status: violated  # 04c7
    priority: 2  # 04c7
    parent:  # 04c7
    tags:  # 04c7
    - catalogue  # 04c7
    - adr_0061  # 04c7
    isbefore: []  # 04c7
    duplicate_of: []  # 04c7
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 04c7
    pr_ref:  # 04c7
    description: "Found 2026-10-11 by code reading while fixing the taint flag/claims-file analogue (PR #1542); NOT yet reproduced live. function_summaries/__init__.py load_function_summaries: _rank returns 2 for any path in user_channel_files('function_summaries') before asking declares_community, so a channel file still carrying provenance: community is stamped user_supplied=True (never community=True), wins name collisions over built-in rows, and survives include_community=False (only rank-1 files are dropped). ADR-0061 ruling 3 ('a community file copied into your config home stays community') and ruling 2 (a community terminating summary never closes a branch) are violated for this channel. cli._loaded_catalogue_files also lists function_summaries.d files unconditionally. Fix direction: partition channel files by declares_community like taint.split_community_files; community ones rank 1 (adds only, community=True), dropped under --no-default-overlays and disclosed under omitted_community_overlays with family. Related, disclosure-only: a community io_primitives overlay named by --io-primitives is still listed under the text USER-SUPPLIED block and sets user_supplied=true while tiers lists it as community (the taint arm now uses named_community_files)."  # 04c7
    fields:  # 04c7
      statement: "A function-summary file's tier is its provenance line wherever it sits: a community file in function_summaries.d only adds, never closes a branch, and --no-default-overlays omits it."  # 04c7
      root_cause: "load_function_summaries' _rank returns 2 (user) for every function_summaries.d path before consulting declares_community, so the provenance line is never read for channel files."  # 04c7
